    "abstract": "Parts figure for the stabiliser box upper panel, showing the stiffener sections, the rib 6 splice plate in both thicknesses and the obsolete outboard stringer deleted by the extended run.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure shows the stabiliser box upper panel structure between ribs four and nine, with the stiffener sections, the rib six splice plate and the outboard stringer.",
      "figure_note": "Sheet 1 shows the upper panel from inside the box looking up, with rib positions marked. Items 20 and 20A are the splice plate thicknesses; the thicker plate at item 20 has the two row fastener pattern and is only used with the extended stiffener run at item 10. The stringer at item 30 is deleted by the extended run and now carries a pre-modification effectivity; until this issue it was shown for every aircraft, and a shop working a modified panel could order a stringer the standard does not use and find nothing to fit it to. Its holes are filled with oversize interference fasteners, which are not shown on this figure."
    },
